  "checks": [
    "Real desktop pane, persisted homepage/search settings and a sandboxed remote page without Node or an opener",
    "Switching tabs hides the native surface; Reading links open Web viewer and separate panes do not share website cookies",
    "Pointer navigation, native back/forward and reload, Ctrl+F and actual find-in-page matches",
    "New-window links stay contained; file links, vault-service navigation and redirects are blocked; no vault token reaches pages",
    "Configured search safely encodes input; a full Electron/.NET restart restores URL, title, settings and unknown nested leaf state",
    "Disable/enable and disabled process restart preserve unavailable leaf state, remove owned commands/ribbon and release browser contents; original workspace/settings data survive",
    "History records successful main-frame and same-document visits, skips consecutive reloads, subframes, blank/error pages and redirect intermediates",
    "History pane searches titles and URLs, reopens a saved address in an isolated browser tab and is reused by toolbar Ctrl+H",
    "Record visits control durably pauses and resumes automatic history without deleting saved visits",
    "Per-visit removal works; a real external edit invalidates a reviewed clear and its exact bytes survive",
    "History, paused recording, search and opaque pane state survive full process restarts; disable removes commands and restores the retained pane on re-enable",
    "Cancel leaves history untouched; confirmed clear removes visits while preserving the recording preference, BOM and opaque configuration fields",
    "Unsupported externally written history is retained during reads and automatic visits; original workspace and Web viewer settings remain byte-identical",
    "Reader extracts the loaded article in an isolated world, retains Unicode/headings/code/tables/captions, omits navigation/active content and returns to identical source DOM, input, scroll, cookies and history",
    "Reader has an opaque sandbox without Node/editor access, enforces its script CSP, ignores page-world prototype spoofing and preserves native URL/token boundaries",
    "Find searches the displayed reader text with previous/next selection; safe links navigate and re-extract, and the owned reader command toggles the actual view",
    "Short/non-article and oversized pages fail visibly without losing browsing; strict source CSP is supported and rapid cancellation/return leaves no reader frame",
    "Reader mode and opaque leaf state persist through a full Electron/.NET restart and rebuild from the newly loaded source page",
    "Disable/disabled restart/re-enable retains reader intent, removes owned command/frames, closes native source contents and preserves original settings/workspace bytes",
    "Clipping previews the isolated loaded article as literal Markdown with headings/lists/quotes/code/tables/links/Unicode/source metadata; Cancel writes nothing and retains original DOM/input/cookies/history without refetching images or sending vault tokens",
    "The save-to-vault command works from Reader, honors an edited nested Unicode path, creates the exact reviewed UTF-8 Markdown, emits one vault create event and opens the saved note",
    "External BOM/CRLF file and folder collisions never overwrite; invalid/traversal/configuration/reserved paths fail with the preview retained, a corrected destination succeeds and new suggestions avoid existing paths",
    "Same-URL navigation invalidates the reviewed clip and disables Save; actual vault switches discard the preview and a retained obsolete dialog cannot create a note in either vault",
    "Short/non-article, oversized source and excessive table pages explain failure with Save disabled and browsing restored; strict website CSP still permits isolated clipping",
    "Previews are transient across full process restarts; disable/disabled restart/re-enable cleans up dialogs, commands and native contents while retaining saved notes, external bytes, clipping settings and original workspace data",
    "Real toolbar zoom changes the native page's device-pixel ratio and viewport to 130% while preserving source DOM/input/cookies/load count/history and the editor shell scale",
    "Independent same-origin tabs keep separate native zoom; owned commands change only the active tab, and returning to a tab retains its percentage",
    "Native zoom reapplies across same-origin and cross-origin navigation, reload, back and forward without changing a second tab's scale",
    "Reader zoom changes actual heading geometry, retains opaque-frame/token isolation and Find, handles Reader/toolbar keyboard input once, clamps rapid commands at 50–300% and resets both surfaces without scaling the editor",
    "Per-tab native/Reader zoom and opaque leaf fields survive full enabled/disabled process restarts; disable removes all three commands/controls and releases native contents before re-enable restores the actual scales",
    "Invalid persisted factors leave the current view untouched, modals release native zoom accelerators, and real vault switches preserve per-tab zoom without leaking commands/state or rewriting original settings/workspace bytes",
    "Real Block ads settings and bundled EasyList cancel both native script requests before they reach the server; normal scripts and the same ad URL as XHR still load, with exactly two blocked requests and no vault access",
    "Saving the setting updates both visible and hidden native sessions for future requests, without reloading or removing existing scripts; per-tab counts and unknown vault settings remain independent and intact",
    "Counts retain blocked requests across hash changes and reset for actual document loads, reload, back and forward without treating denied vault requests as advertisements",
    "Full enabled and disabled process restarts restore the saved Boolean before loading page resources, preserve opaque tab fields and ignore an unrelated leaf field with the same name",
    "Invalid native IPC cannot mutate protection; disabling releases every page and counter, and re-enabling restores filtering with fresh ephemeral storage and no page access to Node",
    "Real vault switches replace each native session's filtering setting, restore the original enabled tabs, preserve both vaults' settings/note/original-workspace bytes and never expose a vault token to fixture requests",
    "Real keyboard-operated font/width settings change computed fonts and article geometry in place, retain article/frame identity and opaque settings, and preserve source DOM/input/scroll/cookies/history without requests or materializing defaults on open",
    "Saved preferences update hidden and visible Reader frames, and a held real native extraction uses the latest saved preferences when its presentation becomes ready"
